# Lane rs_rows, second pass: re-render every direct family in the ruled trace grammar

Read and obey \`$R/orch_tools/CODEX_BUILD_COMMON_20261115.md\` first. Then read your own \`STATUS.md\`, \`out/ROWS_REPORT.md\` and first brief \`BRIEF.md\` in this folder (\`$R/rs_rows\`), and the design ruling \`$TR\` (945 lines; read lines 1 to 417 whole, the appendices as needed). The ruling is adopted. Its sections 2.1 (trace grammar and the numbers a trace may contain), 2.2 (form per question type, with proposed renderings), 2.3 (facing-direction pairs without tools) and 2.4 (changes for this lane) are your specification. Two points it leaves to the user proceed on its defaults (2.9): a direct trace may cite one first-seen or best-view frame per object, never an exhaustive list; a 3D-box row keeps one Locate line before its JSON.

## Build, in this order (one RESULT event after each)
1. **Grammar validator** \`work/trace_grammar.py\` with tests: accepts only Locate, Relate, Step and Call lines; a direct row that contains a call tag or \`<tool_response>\` fails; a trace that contains a number outside the allowed set of 2.1 fails; an empty think block fails; an answer restated without any Locate, Relate or Step line fails. The integration lane will adopt this file, so give it no dependency outside the standard library and document its entry point.
2. **Your four families**, as 2.4 rules: facing (67,970) as direct toward/away pairs per 2.3; totals (2,335) as direct rows with instance lists and an explicit sum; units (24,628) as program rows in the sealed ground-form event schema with masked responses and the \`<answer>\` ending; recovery rebuilt on the routed types (absolute distance, room, camera) with the runtime's own status text from simulated misses at the measured rate, every row ending in a direct answer, no refusal row, no operator-fault status. Keep the program rendering of facing as an unadmitted kit under \`out/kits/\`.
3. **The sealed leg's direct families**, which the ruling found in breach: the rows that state a measurement with no derivation (direction easy, medium and hard, relative distance, object size; 95.0 rows per step) and the answer-only rows (route planning 9,404 rows; 3D-box labels 4,308 rows). Re-render each from the values its row already holds, in the grammar, following the proposed renderings of 2.2. Find the rows from \`$R/leg_s1_tree/out/ADMITTED_TYPE_HISTOGRAM_07ca49df.md\`, \`ROWS_FIVE_PER_TYPE_07ca49df.md\`, \`NO_FLAG_MIX.md\` and the pool they name; if a pool's row payloads are not on this node, say exactly which files are missing and render what is here. Counting and appearance-order rows already list frames: check them against the grammar and re-render only what fails.
Keep row identity, provenance, scene exclusions and the paraphrase variety; build a paraphrase bank so that one template does not dominate a type (report the share of the most common opening line per type).

## Prove on CPU
Every delivered row passes the validator; labels recomputed from geometry for facing; for each re-rendered sealed family, the answer is byte-identical to the sealed row's answer and the question is unchanged; per type the answer distribution before and after is identical; mutation tests for each validator rule; line coverage of the renderers and validator.

## Deliver
\`out/rows_r2/<family>/\` with manifests, \`out/SAMPLES_R2.md\` (12 fixed-seed rows per family, including each re-rendered sealed family), \`out/ROWS_REPORT_R2.md\`, an updated design record, RESULT events as the common rules say. The first-pass rows under \`out/rows\` stay in place, unadmitted. Do not edit any tree; another lane integrates.
EOF
cat > $R/rs_tree/BRIEF2.md <<EOF
# Lane rs_tree, second pass: make the integration tree enforce the ruled trace forms

Read and obey \`$R/orch_tools/CODEX_BUILD_COMMON_20261115.md\` first (your lane may hold 2 GB). Then read your own \`STATUS.md\`, \`out/TREE_REPORT.md\`, \`out/PRELAUNCH_CARD_DRAFT.md\` and first brief \`BRIEF.md\` in this folder (\`$R/rs_tree\`), and the design ruling \`$TR\` (read lines 1 to 417 whole). The ruling is adopted. It found that your first pass (\`work/tree_r1/student_pilot/carrier_c1_routing.py:813-834\`) admits the row builder's rows as direct rows with \`tool_output_spans=[]\`, which supervises calls and responses as plain text and would train program behaviour on direction and counting.

## Build
1. **Contract.** A direct target must pass the grammar validator that lane \`rs_rows\` is writing (\`$R/rs_rows/work/trace_grammar.py\`; if it does not exist yet, implement the rules of the ruling's section 2.1 and reconcile with that file when it appears, keeping one copy in the tree with its source hash): no call tag, no \`<tool_response>\`, no number outside the allowed set, no empty think block. Program rows enter only through the event path whose response spans are masked (\`tree_s1/student_pilot/carrier_c1_routing.py:467-468\`), only for the allowlisted types (absolute distance, room size, camera displacement, camera movement direction, camera rotation), and end in \`<answer>\`. Tests must show that the first-pass rows under \`$R/rs_rows/out/rows/facing\` and \`totals\` are now refused and that a sealed program row is still accepted.
2. **Intake interface.** One documented entry that takes a row manifest from \`$R/rs_rows/out/rows_r2/<family>/\` and from the coverage lists of \`$R/rs_cover/out/lists/\`, validates, applies scene exclusions, and reports per-type admitted and refused counts with reasons. Run it on whatever exists when you reach this step.
3. **Contract patches.** Apply the reviewed second-pass patches of \`$R/rs_contracts/out/PATCH_*_r2.diff\` if \`$R/rs_contracts/out/CONTRACTS_REPORT_R2.md\` exists when you reach this step; if not, say so and leave a single script that applies them later. Never apply the first-pass \`level_basis\` heading switch.
4. **Open gates from your first pass.** (a) Evidence that the geometry tower's training scenes exclude the benchmark and held-out development scenes: search the records listed in \`/data2/jjyeung/agent_project_data/distill_design/INDEX.md\` (single file, then the records it names) and \`$R/gf1_fusion/out/RECORD.md\`; state what is shown and what is not. (b) What a real per-rank first-batch forward needs that this node lacks (frame stores, sizes, where they live), and the smallest CPU job on the machine that holds the frames that would prove it.
5. **Pre-launch card** updated to the ruling: the per-step mix by type and trace form (direct qualitative, program with ground-truth response, program with deployed response, fallback), with the 288-row step the sealed leg actually used and the exact census in \`$R/rs_cover/out/CENSUS_LEG.md\`; the registered reads F1 to F4 of the ruling's section 2.7 with their thresholds; the stages (alignment trains only the geometry adapter with the language model frozen; then full fine-tuning).

## Deliver
Updated \`work/tree_r1\`, \`out/TREE_R1.diff\` and hashes, \`out/TREE_REPORT_R2.md\`, \`out/PRELAUNCH_CARD_DRAFT.md\`, tests, changed-line coverage, the design record, RESULT events as the common rules say. Nothing outside this lane is edited; no launch.
EOF
cat > $R/o3_cache/BRIEF.md <<EOF
# Lane o3_cache: do tool responses reveal their own errors, and a kit that renders deployed responses on training scenes (CPU study now; GPU kit built and rehearsed, not launched)

Read and obey \`$R/orch_tools/CODEX_BUILD_COMMON_20261115.md\` first.

## Why
The project trains a 9B spatial vision-language model whose routed question types call its own perception tools. Until now every program row was trained on responses computed from ground-truth instances, while at inference the same calls return predicted masks, a frozen selector and the model's own depth and pose heads, with real failures. The adopted design ruling \`$TR\` (read its sections 1b, 1c, 2.6, 2.7 and 2.8) says: for absolute distance and room size, render training responses from the deployed pipeline on training scenes, keep rows whose response agrees with ground truth (trust rows) and rows whose response is a real failure and whose trace then answers directly (fallback rows), and leave out the silently wrong ones. No cache of deployed responses on training scenes exists.

## Part 1: cue study, CPU only (stage 1 of the ruling's section 2.6)
On the existing caches (\`$R/grd_selector\` 84 selector-training scans; \`$R/devs1_masks/cache_r1\` and \`$R/mask_recall\` for the development captures; read their STATUS.md and run cards first), test whether anything printed in a tool response separates right from wrong program answers: the status, the number of frames, the spread, a missing size, disagreement between two calls. Report AUROC per cue and per question type with a bootstrap interval over scenes, the best single rule, and the score of "program, fall back to direct when the cue fires" against program-only and direct-only on every item available. If nothing beyond the failure status reaches AUROC 0.65, say so plainly. Keep development scenes and selector-training scans separate in every table. Also do the counting census the ruling lists in 2.10: the edits between the deployed instance list and ground truth on the 84-scan cache.

## Part 2: the cache kit
Build, and rehearse on CPU with stand-ins only at the GPU boundary, a kit that renders deployed responses for the absolute-distance and room rows of the training pool (about 2,189 scenes): the geometry pass (tower plus the step-544 model's own heads), the mask proposal pass at the frozen setting, the selector, the response renderer the runtime uses, and the filter that labels each row trust, fallback or left out (the ruling's tolerance: within 15% of ground truth and the accepted masks matching the ground-truth instance). Reuse the code of the development-set cache (\`$R/devs1_masks\`, \`$R/devs1_tower\`, \`$R/legs1_routed/out2\`) and the native reader's geometry path (\`$R/evalx/work/milestone/native_package_s24_05/sources\`, read-only). Find where the training frames and the step-544 export (21.6 GB) live from the records (\`$R/leg_s1_review/CONTINUATION_FACTS_20261114.md\`, \`$R/orchard_cp2/STATUS.md\`, \`/data2/jjyeung/agent_project_data/DATA_MAP.md\`), and propose where the kit runs (Trinity cards of 49 GB under vnice, or Orchard H100s where the leg trained), with bytes to move by which route, GPU hours from recorded timings, and what is untested there. Move nothing and launch nothing.

## Deliver
\`out/CUE_STUDY.md\` (first RESULT event when it is done), \`out/CACHE_KIT_REPORT.md\` with the launch packet (exact commands, cards, expected time, stop command, disk needed), the kit under \`work/kit\`, tests and line coverage, the design record, RESULT events as the common rules say.
EOF
